Use the real name in which's option errors from the shell.
The standalone shell passes "Which" as argv[0] to tell which that it
may report applets. getopt() names the program by argv[0], so an
unknown option gave "Which: unknown option -- x". Put the applet name
back in argv[0] once the flag has been read.

---
 debianutils/which.c |    3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/debianutils/which.c
+++ b/debianutils/which.c
@@ -44,6 +44,9 @@
 #if ENABLE_PLATFORM_MINGW32 && ENABLE_FEATURE_SH_STANDALONE
 	/* 'Which' in argv[0] indicates we were run from a standalone shell */
 	int sh_standalone = argv[0][0] == 'W';
+
+	if (sh_standalone) /* getopt prints argv[0] in its messages */
+		argv[0] = (char *)applet_name;
 #endif
 
 	env_path = getenv("PATH");
